<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head><title>Not found</title><%- include("partials/head") %></head>
<body class="auth-page">
  <div class="auth-card">
    <h1>Not found</h1>
    <%# Deliberately does NOT say "expired". Install links never expire — there
        is no TTL, no retention job and no lifecycle rule anywhere in this
        service, so a link that stops working was deleted, never timed out.
        The old copy ("This link has expired, been deleted, or never existed")
        made a deletion read as an expiry and sent someone looking for an
        expiry setting that does not exist. %>
    <p class="muted">
      This build has been deleted, or this link was never valid.
      Install links do not expire on their own.
    </p>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
